{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 14, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark hark good traveler to Japan’s fair isle\nLet mine quill weave thee a path most noble and bright\nThy journey shall start with a touch of old Tokyo’s might\n\nOn the morn of thine arrival do stand in Asakusa’s glade\nWhere Senso-ji’s temple doth gleam in light most radiant made\nBow thy head to the gods in prayer and seek their blessing sweet\nThen stroll through streets where lanterns do dance on the evening’s fleet.\n\nTo Ueno’s garden next thou shalt repair\nWhere cherry blossoms in spring do bloom with grace most rare\nDo sit beneath their boughs and watch the world go by\nWhile geisha and samurai in memory’s eye do lie.\n\nOnward to Shinjuku let thy feet now tread\nWhere neon and chaos in splendid discord spread\nIn Golden Gai’s lanes do wander through alleys small\nWhere bars with names like secrets hold stories to enthrall.\n\nThen take the train to Kyoto’s ancient keep\nWhere temples of gold and bamboo groves do weep\nVisit Kinkaku-ji where the sun on its halls doth play\nAnd Fushimi Inari where foxes do lead the way.\n\nTo Arashiyama’s bridge do now hasten thy gait\nWhere the river flows soft beneath the moonlight’s pale light\nAnd in the bamboo forest let thy spirit be still\nAs whispers of old Japan in the wind do spill.\n\nA night in Gion’s quarter with lanterns aglow\nWhere maiko’s giggles and sake cups flow\nDo watch their world of dance and ritual precise\nA fleeting glimpse of Japan’s soul most wise.\n\nThence to Nara’s plain where deer with eyes like coins\nDo wander the paths where the Great Buddha grins\nBow to Todai-ji’s giant in stone so tall\nAnd let the past in its shadow upon thee enthrall.\n\nReturn to Osaka where street food’s feast doth call\nTry takoyaki and okonomiyaki’s thrall\nIn Dotonbori’s glow where signs in English do cheer\nThe city’s night alive with laughter and cheer.\n\nTo Hiroshima’s park where the flame shall not burn\nBut memories stand in the museum’s stern yearn\nThen to Miyajima where the torii gate doth rise\nFrom the sea’s embrace ‘neath the floating skies.\n\nIn Kanazawa’s domain where samurai once did tread\nVisit Kenrokuen where gardens spread\nLike paintings of old where seasons in layers unfold\nAnd gold leaf on gates where the past in splendor is told.\n\nTo Takayama’s streets where time moves slow\nWhere old wooden houses stand proud and still\nDo sip sake with farmers and watch the world go by\nIn a town where Japan’s heart in simplicity doth lie.\n\nOn thy final days in Tokyo’s whirl once more\nDo climb Mount Fuji’s view from Kamakura’s shore\nOr in Odaiba’s future where the Rainbow Bridge does gleam\nTake heed of thy time and let not its splendor deem.\n\nOn the eve of thy departure stand at Shinjuku’s cross\nWhere last-minute shopping and souvenirs do toss\nBut pause and reflect on this land so fair\nWhere ancient and modern in endless dance do pair.\n\nLet thy heart bear the memories of temples and trains\nOf geisha and gods and the food that sustains\nGood speed on thy journey and may thy path ever be bright\nFarewell fair traveler to Japan’s wondrous sight.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.16029712557792664}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.003225721186026931}, {"token": " h", "logprob": -1.5492585897445679}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.0038220465648919344}, {"token": " good", "logprob": -0.4081418216228485}, {"token": " travel", "logprob": -0.351406067609787}, {"token": "er", "logprob": -0.0007333449902944267}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -2.4611754417419434}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -1.1534624099731445}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.2761080861091614}, {"token": " fair", "logprob": -0.14014331996440887}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -1.8376728296279907}, {"token": "le", "logprob": -0.0384613461792469}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.5947836637496948}, {"token": "Let", "logprob": -1.6601130962371826}, {"token": " mine